cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the article."
title: "Personalized kinematic constraint-based drift correction for 3D golf swing trajectory monitoring with a wrist-worn IMU"
authors:
  - family-names: Park
    given-names: Guen-a
    affiliation: "Korea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-21"
repository-code: "https://github.com/guen-a-park/golf-swing-imu-drift-correction"
abstract: >-
  MATLAB and Python code for reconstructing the three-dimensional wrist
  trajectory of a golf swing from a single wrist-worn inertial measurement
  unit, using a subject-specific kinematic constraint obtained once from
  monocular video and thereafter inferred from the IMU signals alone.
keywords:
  - inertial measurement unit
  - drift correction
  - golf swing
  - monocular video
  - human motion analysis
